Environment: macOS darwin 25.5.0 arm64, local dev profile, UTC

WHAT CHANGED (audit class before: WIRED — the pipeline existed in the
tools crate with real file I/O tests, but the production fs.read tool
bypassed it entirely: binary files returned as lossy UTF-8 strings)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
- build_worktree_registry constructs the MediaPipeline (content-
  addressed objects under the worktree's untracked .modbit/objects;
  8 MiB ingest budget; the revision-bound diff never sees the objects).
- fs.read: PNG/JPEG/PDF reads (real magic-byte detection) ingest
  through the pipeline and return a typed media envelope {kind, mime,
  byte_length, sha256, object_ref} plus a bounded [media: ...]
  descriptor as the conversation content — never lossy binary; text
  reads stay plain.

